 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Mechanism:** Werkzeug `LocalProxy` objects backed by a `ContextVar`. Each proxy looks up the current context on every access, so it resolves per thread/coroutine.\n\n**In `src/tessel/globals.py`:**\n- `_app_var: ContextVar[AppContext]` (line 40) holds the current `AppContext`. It is set and reset as contexts are pushed and popped, in `src/tessel/ctx.py`.\n- `active_app` is `LocalProxy(_app_var, \"app\")`, so it resolves to `AppContext.app`, the `Tessel` instance.\n- `g` is `LocalProxy(_app_var, \"g\")`, so it resolves to `AppContext.g`, an `_AppCtxGlobals`.\n- `request` is `LocalProxy(_app_var, \"request\")`, so it resolves to `AppContext.request`, a `Request`.\n- `app_ctx` and `session` follow the same pattern, using `AppContext` itself and `AppContext.session`.\n\nIf no context is bound, the proxy raises a `RuntimeError` with the \"Working outside of application context\" message (or \"request context\" for `request` and `session`).\n\nRequest data lives on the same `AppContext` as everything else, which is why `request_ctx` is deprecated in favour of `app_ctx`.",
